<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>Winter Sports Travel: One Van for Basketball, Wrestling, and Hockey Weekends</h1>
<p>Saturday tournaments, Sunday duals, and a lot of winter miles. Here&#x27;s the math on one van instead of six carpools.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>Fall sports wrapped up, and the winter calendar is already full: basketball tournaments, wrestling duals and invitationals, club volleyball, youth hockey. That's a lot of Saturdays on I-94 and Highway 54, often in the dark and often in snow. One rented van gets the roster there together, on time, with one driver who knows the route.</p>
<h2>The math on one van</h2>
<p>The <a href="/van-rental.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">15-passenger van</a> is $135/day plus $0.10/mile. A Saturday tournament 75 miles away is a 150-mile round trip: $135 plus $15, or $150 before taxes and fees. Split across 12 athletes, that's $12.50 each, which is less than most families spend on gas driving separately.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Two-day tournament with an overnight:</strong> two days is $270 plus mileage.</li>
<li><strong>Holiday tournament stretch:</strong> for local renters, the weekly rate is $750 with unlimited miles.</li>
<li><strong>Smaller squad or coaching staff:</strong> the <a href="/blog/7-passenger-minivan-rental-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">7-passenger minivan</a> is $78/day plus $0.10/mile.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pack for a full van</h2>
<p>When every seat is filled, there's less room for gear. Pack soft duffels instead of hard cases, keep the aisle clear, and put the team bag of balls or the mat tape where it won't slide. If the equipment list is long, send it in a parent's car and keep the athletes in the van.</p>
<h2>Who drives</h2>
<p>Drivers must be 21 or older with a valid U.S. driver's license, and there's no young-driver fee. The renter brings a Visa, Mastercard, or Discover credit or debit card linked to a checking account, and proof of full-coverage auto insurance. Riverside doesn't sell insurance. Check your school district's or club's policy on who's allowed to drive athletes before you book.</p>
<h2>Winter road sense</h2>
<p>Leave earlier than you think. Check <a href="https://511wi.gov" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;" rel="noopener">511 Wisconsin</a> the night before and the morning of, give the van extra stopping room, and keep speeds down on overpasses. A late weigh-in beats an accident.</p>
<p><strong>Call or text 715-396-1466</strong> with your schedule. We have one 15-passenger van, and tournament weekends go fast. Our hours are Monday to Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM, Saturday 8:00 AM to noon, and Sunday closed. After-hours drop-off returns are available.</p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How much does it cost to rent a van for a team tournament?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>The 15-passenger van is $135/day plus $0.10/mile. A 150-mile round trip costs about $150 before taxes and fees, or $12.50 per player across 12 athletes. Local renters can book a week for $750 with unlimited miles.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Can a parent or coach drive the rental van?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes, if they are 21 or older with a valid U.S. driver&#x27;s license. Check your school or club&#x27;s policy on who may drive athletes.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Is there a minivan option for a small team?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. The 7-passenger minivan is $78/day plus $0.10/mile, or $450/week with unlimited miles for local renters.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How far ahead should we book for tournament season?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>As soon as the schedule is out. There is one 15-passenger van, and winter tournament weekends book early.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
